module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.memo_entry_occurrence_ids_reminted_after_a_rejected_attempt

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data memo_entry_occurrence_ids_reminted_after_a_rejected_attempt: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "memo_entry_occurrence_ids_reminted_after_a_rejected_attempt" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**the v2 parser hands out an occurrence id a stored memo entry still holds** (INVALID STATE: two nodes of one parse tree carry the same minted OccurrenceId, and the span index answers for only one of them). A rejected attempt returns no provenance, so the caller resumes from the allocator it held before the attempt, but the memo entries the attempt stored are kept. When the continuing parse mints before it asks the same (production, position) again, it mints the stored ids a second time, and the hit's frame replay (`v2.std.provenance` `span_index_adopt`, base entry wins) keeps the new entry, so the replayed node answers for another node's span. HARM: every consumer of the span index reads a wrong locus or none -- a diagnostic located at the wrong text, and `v2.compiler.reference_conservation` unable to measure the module (`AtomExtentUnreadable`), which `conserved_normalize` refuses.",
    "WHERE, cited by symbol. `v2.compiler.parse` `parse_expr_not_predicate_attempt` (either arm), `parse_choice_ordered_backtrack`, `parse_expr_optional` and `parse_expr_repeat_step` resumed with the pre-attempt `ParseProvenanceState`, while `parse_table_insert` kept the entry. A lookahead is the shape that makes the window certain: it parses input the continuing parse reaches only after minting. gunbc#13056 put one in every match arm body (`v2.extdeps.languages.dag` `dag_grammar_match_arm_stmt_body_statement`, the guard `!(pattern =>)`), so from the second arm on the arm's pattern was served from the guard's entry with reminted ids; the `_` of `_ => 2` shared its id with a derived conjunction.",
    "RECEIPTS. `v2.test.claim.body_lowering.single_arm_match` `two_arm_match_still_accepts_holds` and `three_arm_match_keeps_every_arm_holds` red from fd30a502f5 (gunbc#13056): one `AtomExtentUnreadable` per arm after the first, read by a temporary probe over `v2.compiler.reference_conservation` `reference_conservation_of_subject` (not landed). The earlier triage receipt on `match_arms_after_the_second_are_dropped_at_v2_body_lowering` read the refusal as a dropped atom; the row is `conservation_reason_unmeasured`, no reference was dropped, and body lowering was not the boundary.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. Not `match_arms_after_the_second_are_dropped_at_v2_body_lowering`: every arm is in the normalized tree; what is wrong is the identity the parser gave one atom. Not the abandoned-path merge `v2.test.provenance.parse_memo_frame_replay` `parse_memo_hit_carries_no_abandoned_path_provenance` pins: there a hit imported ids it did not return; here the ids it returns were handed out again.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor (silent wrongness: the parse is Accepted with an identity that answers for two nodes, visible only to a reader that resolves loci). REPAIRED AT THE ALLOCATOR, the earliest unjustified boundary (DESIGN 6b): the provenance a rejected attempt discards was never entitled to rewind ids the kept memo retains. `ParseTableRealization` `retained_alloc` carries the allocator high-water of every accepted entry the table stores or serves (`parse_table_retaining`; the seed serves entries across parses of one stream, so a hit retains as an insert does), and every resume after a rejection goes through `parse_prov_resume_after_rejection`. RUNG NOW: mechanically preventable -- the discriminating claim below is red against the parser before this change and green after it, and the resume sites are an enumeration a new combinator could miss. CEILING: structurally guaranteed. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: an allocator threaded through the state that survives rejection (the parse table) instead of the provenance a rejection discards, so no combinator can resume from a rewound allocator because none holds one.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.provenance.parse_memo_frame_replay", decl_name: "parse_memo_hit_after_a_lookahead_resolves_like_a_memo_free_parse", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_lowering.single_arm_match", decl_name: "two_arm_match_still_accepts_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
